  "financeRulesBody": "Monthly cost reference: unexpired prepaid renewal prices divided by the cycle length in months, plus metered monthly estimates. Prepaid services are excluded on and after their expiry date. Missing dates or costs are marked unknown.\n\nRemaining value: the current renewal price prorated by unused days in each known service period. The start date is included and the end date excluded. Future whole periods count at full price; ended periods count as 0. Not applicable to metered billing; unknown when details are insufficient. This is not a refundable amount or sale price.\n\nRenewal forecast: assumes continued renewal at the current price and cycle. The next 30 days includes today and the following 29 days. Six months means the rest of this month and the next five calendar months. Expired services are not projected forward. Metered bills are excluded. Local usage plans do not change the forecast.\n\nPayments in the last 30 days: recorded payments from today and the preceding 29 days. The all-groups scope retains payments for archived servers and counts each independent account bill once. Account bills are not allocated to groups.\n\nWhen cross-currency rates are missing, only convertible amounts are totaled, while original-currency subtotals are retained. Exact amounts are summed before rounding to minor units. Reference conversions are not actual charges.",
